{
  "name": "Automated Research Paper Summarizer",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "summarize-paper",
        "responseMode": "lastNode",
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [250, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "={{ $json.body.url }}",
        "options": {
          "response": { "response": { "responseFormat": "text" } }
        }
      },
      "name": "Fetch Paper",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [470, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\nconst html = items[0].json.data || items[0].json.body || '';\n\n// Strip HTML tags and extract text\nconst text = html.toString().replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ').replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').trim();\n\n// Try to extract common sections\nconst sections = {};\nconst sectionNames = ['abstract', 'introduction', 'methodology', 'results', 'discussion', 'conclusion'];\n\nfor (const section of sectionNames) {\n  const regex = new RegExp(section + '[:\\\\s]*([\\\\s\\\\S]{100,2000}?)(?=' + sectionNames.filter(s => s !== section).join('|') + '|$)', 'i');\n  const match = text.match(regex);\n  if (match) sections[section] = match[1].trim().substring(0, 2000);\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    url: $('Webhook').item.json.body.url,\n    fullText: text.substring(0, 8000),\n    sections,\n    extractedSections: Object.keys(sections),\n    charCount: text.length\n  }\n}];"
      },
      "name": "Extract Paper Sections",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [690, 300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "resource": "chat",
        "model": "gpt-4o-mini",
        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=Summarize this research paper. Provide:\n1. **Title** (infer from text)\n2. **Key Finding** (1-2 sentences)\n3. **Methodology** (brief)\n4. **Results Summary**\n5. **Limitations**\n6. **Practical Implications**\n\nPaper text:\n{{ $json.fullText }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "temperature": 0.3,
          "maxTokens": 2000
        }
      },
      "name": "OpenAI Summarize",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 1.8,
      "position": [910, 300],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": { "id": "", "name": "" }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $('Webhook').item.json.body.email || '' }}",
        "subject": "=Paper Summary: {{ $('Extract Paper Sections').item.json.url }}",
        "message": "={{ $json.message.content }}",
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Gmail Send Summary",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [1130, 200],
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": { "id": "", "name": "" }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "operation": "append",
        "sheetId": { "__rl": true, "mode": "list", "value": "" },
        "columns": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "url": "={{ $('Extract Paper Sections').item.json.url }}",
            "summary": "={{ $json.message.content }}",
            "char_count": "={{ $('Extract Paper Sections').item.json.charCount }}",
            "sections_found": "={{ $('Extract Paper Sections').item.json.extractedSections.join(', ') }}",
            "date": "={{ new Date().toISOString() }}"
          }
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "name": "Log to Sheets",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleSheets",
      "typeVersion": 4.5,
      "position": [1130, 400],
      "credentials": {
        "googleSheetsOAuth2Api": { "id": "", "name": "" }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Automated Research Paper Summarizer\n\nFetches a research paper from a URL, extracts key sections, and uses OpenAI to produce a structured summary. Results are emailed and logged to Google Sheets.\n\n**Setup:**\n1. Configure Gmail and Google Sheets credentials\n2. Add OpenAI API key\n3. POST to webhook: `{\"url\": \"paper_url\", \"email\": \"recipient@example.com\"}`"
      },
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [230, 80]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Webhook": {
      "main": [
        [{ "node": "Fetch Paper", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]
      ]
    },
    "Fetch Paper": {
      "main": [
        [{ "node": "Extract Paper Sections", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]
      ]
    },
    "Extract Paper Sections": {
      "main": [
        [{ "node": "OpenAI Summarize", "type": "main", "index": 0 }]
      ]
    },
    "OpenAI Summarize": {
      "main": [
        [
          { "node": "Gmail Send Summary", "type": "main", "index": 0 },
          { "node": "Log to Sheets", "type": "main", "index": 0 }
        ]
      ]
    }
  }
}